<!-- wp:mbn-theme/hero-section {"eyebrowText":"Practice Areas","mainHeading":"Personal Injury Accidents","subheading":"","overlayImageUrl":"https://hastingsandhastings.dev.local/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/img-fg-video-overlay.webp","overlayImageId":8556,"showCtaBar":false,"backgroundImageUrl":"https://hastingsandhastings.dev.local/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/img-hero-bg-car-accident-injuries.jpg","backgroundImageId":10037,"contentJustify":"justify-between","contentVerticalAlign":"items-end","textMaxWidth":"max-w-3xl","showQuickCall":true} /-->

<!-- wp:mbn-theme/practice-area-details {"sections":[{"id":"whyHire-default","type":"whyHire","title":{"heading":"","paragraphs":[""],"backgroundColor":"bg-white"},"data":{"heading":"Why Hire Hastings & Hastings?","subtitle":"If you were injured because of someone else’s negligence, it can be difficult to know what your rights are or what steps to take next. Hastings & Hastings is here to help personal injury victims understand their options and schedule a free consultation with an experienced Arizona personal injury attorney.","features":[{"id":"feature1","title":"Over 90 Years of Combined Experience","description":"Our team has over 90 years of combined experience helping injury victims in Arizona. That experience allows us to guide families through serious and sensitive wrongful death claims with care and focus."},{"id":"feature2","title":"Free Consultations With a Licensed Attorney","description":"When you schedule a free consultation, you will always meet with one of our licensed attorneys. You can ask questions, discuss what happened, and receive legal guidance from someone qualified to advise you."},{"id":"feature3","title":"No Fees Unless We Win","description":"We work on a contingency fee basis, so you don’t pay a dime until we win your case. This allows families to seek legal help without worrying about upfront attorney fees during an already difficult time."}],"photoUrl":"","photoId":0,"badge90YearsUrl":"","badge90YearsId":0,"mapBackgroundUrl":"","mapBackgroundId":0,"badgeNoFeeUrl":"https://hastingsandhastings.dev.local/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/img-founding-atty.jpg","badgeNoFeeId":11049,"freeEvaluationsTitle":"Meet Our Founding Attorney","freeEvaluationsDescription":"<p>Founding attorney David G. Hastings created Hastings & Hastings in 1981. After graduating from the University of Arizona in business administration and law, Mr. Hastings began his legal career working for insurance companies, eventually shifting to represent victims of negligence. Since then, Mr. Hastings has become known as “The Discount King”, nicknamed by the Arizona Business Gazette, because he works hard to save his clients money.</p>\n<p>In addition to working hard to advocate for his clients, Mr. Hastings is involved in local philanthropy. He is involved in supporting organizations such as Special Olympics Arizona and Phoenix Children’s Hospital, as well as helping build homes in Mexico with 1Mission.</p>","millionsRecoveredTitle":"","millionsRecoveredDescription":""}},{"id":"cta1-default","type":"cta","title":{"heading":"","paragraphs":[],"backgroundColor":"bg-light-blue"},"data":{"logoUrl":"","logoId":0,"textureUrl":"","textureId":0,"heading":"Start Your Free Consultation","subtext":"Contact the discount accident lawyers at Hastings and Hastings today.","buttonText":"Start your free consultation now!","buttonUrl":"#contact","phoneLabel":"Call Today","phoneNumber":"(480) 480-2929"}},{"id":"afterAccident-default","type":"afterAccident","title":{"heading":"","paragraphs":[],"backgroundColor":"bg-light-blue"},"data":{"heading":"","splits":[{"id":"split1","text":"<h3 class=\"pad-section-heading\"><span class=\"pad-text-blue\">An Overview </span>of Personal Injury in Arizona</h3>\n<p>Getting hurt because of another person’s negligence does more than just cause unexpected expenses in your life. It also turns your entire life upside down. Damage to your vehicle or other personal property, the inability to work, potential emotional distress, and potential temporary or permanent disability along with the unexpected medical bills impact your mental health along with your relationships.</p>\n<p>If you’re a personal injury victim in Arizona, there’s no doubt that you have several questions. Hastings & Hastings is here to help you get the answers you need. After reading, schedule your free consultation.</p>","imageUrl":"https://hastingsandhastings.dev.local/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/img-personal-injury-1.jpg","imageId":11053,"layout":"text-left"}]}},{"id":"mrc7t2a29d0d8jrude","type":"accidentList","title":{"heading":"<span class=\"pad-text-blue\">What Is Personal Injury</span> in Arizona?","paragraphs":["Personal injury is a broad term that encompasses a large set of circumstances that caused one person to be injured as the result of another person’s actions. This other person’s action or actions is known as negligence. Negligence is one of the elements that is part of a personal injury legal claim."],"backgroundColor":"bg-light-blue"},"data":{"heading":"Examples of personal injury in Arizona include:","backgroundColor":"bg-light-blue","items":[{"label":"Car accidents","url":"#","id":"mrc7ulba183t54cgra7"},{"label":"Truck accidents","url":"#","id":"mrc7uqou1mlhpox13cg"},{"label":"Bicycle accidents","url":"#","id":"mrc7uu7xd9zyqvp9bwp"},{"label":"Pedestrian accidents","url":"#","id":"mrc7uxld05ssn8fmf3bf"},{"label":"Construction accidents","url":"#","id":"mrc7v1tgcfgu0exka7m"},{"label":"Catastrophic accidents","url":"#","id":"mrc7v50o8ofxz688z4b"},{"label":"Slip and fall accidents","url":"#","id":"mrc7v7vepxmc2dbejlb"},{"label":"Wrongful death","url":"#","id":"mrc7vd1m2btpxnb2z9f"},{"label":"Dog bites","url":"#","id":"mrc7vgeo9fm5vl85emm"},{"label":"Motorcycle accidents","url":"#","id":"mrc7vhuc5sl29ktr7y"},{"label":"Product liability injuries","url":"#","id":"mrc7vmlo528erkc4pwj"},{"label":"Brain injuries","url":"#","id":"mrc7vpqpyswqgvrwrsk"}]}},{"id":"insurance-default","type":"insurance","title":{"heading":"","paragraphs":[],"backgroundColor":"bg-light-blue"},"data":{"heading":"Dealing With Insurance Companies","text":"<p>While a personal injury settlement is separate than a property damage settlement (fixing your car), they are very much related. Getting a proper estimate and returning your vehicle to a pre-accident state is essential to demonstrate how much true damage was done to a vehicle. This also aids in showing how you were injured, and the extent of your injuries. Insurance companies often \"low ball\" a client's property damage in an effort to try to minimize and even eliminate a client's personal injury claim. <strong>This is why, at Hastings and Hastings, we always recommend that you speak to an attorney before dealing with any insurance company, including your own.</strong></p>","photoUrl":"","photoId":0}},{"id":"cta2-default","type":"cta","title":{"heading":"","paragraphs":[],"backgroundColor":"bg-light-blue"},"data":{"logoUrl":"","logoId":0,"textureUrl":"","textureId":0,"heading":"Dealing With Insurance? Talk to an Attorney First.","subtext":"Insurance companies may try to minimize your claim. Before accepting an offer or speaking with an adjuster, contact Hastings & Hastings to understand your options.","buttonText":"Request Free Consultation","buttonUrl":"#contact","phoneLabel":"Call Today","phoneNumber":"(480) 480-2929"}},{"id":"liability-default","type":"liability","title":{"heading":"","paragraphs":[],"backgroundColor":"bg-light-blue"},"data":{"heading":"<span class=\"pad-text-blue\">Who is Liable</span> For My Phoenix Car Accident?","subtitle":"If you've been in a car accident, you may be wondering who is liable for the damages. The answer to this question depends on many factors. The following are some of the parties that could be liable for a car accident:","introHeading":"","introText":"","backgroundColor":"bg-white","paddingTop":"","paddingBottom":"","items":[{"id":"liability1","term":"Other Driver Is At Fault","description":"<p>If another driver caused your accident, their insurance company should cover the damages. In some cases, the other driver may not have insurance or their insurance may not be enough to cover the damages.</p><p>If this is the case, you may need to file a lawsuit against the other driver to get the money you deserve. You should also check your own insurance policy to see if you have uninsured/underinsured motorist coverage, which would kick in if the other driver doesn't have enough insurance to cover your damages.</p>"},{"id":"liability2","term":"Both Drivers Are At Fault","description":"<p>In some cases, both drivers may be found at fault for an accident. In Arizona, this situation is governed by something called <a href=\"https://www.azleg.gov/ars/12/02505.htm\">pure comparative negligence</a>.</p><p>For example, let's say that you rear-ended another car, but that driver was sitting at a green light texting. In this case, you would likely be found partially at fault for the accident because you were not paying close enough attention.</p><p>However, the other driver would also be found at fault because they were distracted, which caused you to hit them. The amount of money you can recover from the other driver will be reduced by the percentage that you are at fault. So, if you are 20% at fault and the total damages are $10,000, you can only recover $8,000 – 80% – from the other driver.</p>"},{"id":"liability3","term":"Manufacturer Is At Fault","description":"<p>In some cases, an accident may be caused by a defective part. For example, if your brakes fail and you rear-end another car, it's possible that the brake manufacturer is at fault for the accident. If this is the case, you can file a product liability lawsuit against the manufacturer to recover damages.</p>"}]}},{"id":"compensation-default","type":"compensation","title":{"heading":"","paragraphs":[],"backgroundColor":"bg-light-blue"},"data":{"heading":"<span class=\"pad-text-blue\">Recovering Compensation</span> For My Injury","subtitle":"Here are some of the most common types of compensation you may be entitled to after a car accident:","afterText":"","items":[{"id":"comp1","title":"Medical Expenses","description":"<p>One of the main types of compensation you can recover after a car accident is medical expenses. This includes both past and future expenses related to your injuries. Your medical expenses may include hospitalization, surgery, medication, physical therapy, and any other treatment recommended by your doctor.</p><p>If your injuries are expected to have long-term effects, your lawyer will also take into account long-term future medical costs when negotiating with the insurance company.</p>"},{"id":"comp2","title":"Lost Income","description":"<p>If you miss time from work due to your injuries, you may be able to recover lost income as part of your compensation. This includes not only wages lost while you are out of work but also any reduction in earnings capacity due to long-term effects of your injuries.</p><p>For example, if you can no longer work full-time or perform the same job duties as before the car accident, you may be able to recover damages for lost earning capacity.</p>"},{"id":"comp3","title":"Out-of-Pocket Expenses","description":"<p>In addition to medical expenses and lost income, there are other out-of-pocket expenses that can be included in your compensation. These may include the cost of renting a car while yours is being repaired, childcare expenses while you are receiving medical treatment, and help around the house if you are unable to perform all your usual activities.</p><p>If any property was damaged or destroyed in the accident, you may also be able to recover the cost of replacing it.</p>"},{"id":"comp4","title":"Pain and Suffering","description":"<p>Finally, if you file a personal injury lawsuit, you may also be able to recover damages for pain and suffering caused by your injuries. This type of damage is intended to compensate you for the physical and emotional anguish caused by the accident.</p><p>To prove pain and suffering damages, it is often necessary to present expert testimony from a doctor or other expert witness who can attest to the severity of your injuries and their effects on your life.</p>"}]}},{"id":"attorneys-default","type":"attorneys","title":{"heading":"","paragraphs":[],"backgroundColor":"bg-light-blue"},"data":{"heading":"<span class=\"pad-text-blue\">Our Accident & Injury Attorneys</span> Can Help","text":"<p>At Hastings and Hastings we understand that car accidents can cause all types of injuries. These injuries can range from neck and back pain, to much more severe and permanent injuries, or in the worst case — a fatality. Hastings and Hastings offers over 90 years of combined legal experience in handling all types of accident injuries and we urge you to call now to schedule an appointment to meet with an experienced Phoenix car accident attorney.</p>","photoUrl":"","photoId":0,"badgeCards":[{"id":"badge1","imageUrl":"","imageId":0,"description":"You pay nothing upfront and nothing out of pocket. Hastings & Hastings only gets paid if your case results in a recovery."},{"id":"badge2","imageUrl":"","imageId":0,"description":"Hastings & Hastings is known for its 29% settlement fee, giving clients a more affordable way to get experienced legal representation."},{"id":"badge3","imageUrl":"","imageId":0,"description":"Compared to firms that charge 33%, our lower fee structure gives Hastings & Hastings a meaningful cost advantage."}]}}]} /-->
